      "body": "## Overview\n\nWith `--load-format dummy`, `initialize_single_dummy_weight` fills an FP8 tensor through a full-size FP16 temporary (`uniform_` does not support FP8). For the frozen FP8 Engram tables of DeepSeek-V4.1, that temporary is twice the size of the table. The dummy loader now zeroes these tables in place through a `uint8` view. Tables with an explicit `dummy_weight_value` still use it.\n\nSplit from #62365 by @aoshen02.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `vllm/model_executor/model_loader/dummy_loader.py`: FP8 tensors that carry `engram_vocab_start` (set only on Engram table shards) and no `dummy_weight_value` are zeroed with `tensor.view(torch.uint8).zero_()`. Every other tensor goes through `initialize_single_dummy_weight` as before.\n- `tests/model_executor/test_weight_utils.py`: `test_dummy_engram_table_avoids_full_precision_temporary` (CPU) fails if `torch.empty_like` is called on the table, and checks that other FP8 weights are still randomized.\n\n## Validation\n\nUnit test, GH200 (B300 gives the same counts):\n\n```bash\npytest tests/model_executor/test_weight_utils.py\n```\n\nmain (the same test file on main):\n\n```\ntest_dummy_engram_table_avoids_full_precision_temporary[None]: E AssertionError: Engram FP8 randomization allocates FP16\nFAILED tests/model_executor/test_weight_utils.py::test_dummy_engram_table_avoids_full_precision_temporary[None]\n1 failed, 58 passed in 16.53s\n```\n\nThis PR:\n\n```\n59 passed in 15.95s\n```\n\nPeak memory, B300: one 16 GiB FP8 table (`4194304 x 4096`) with a `uint8` scale column, tagged like an Engram table shard, dummy-loaded on the GPU. Peak allocated memory above the tables during `load_weights`:\n\n```\n# main\npeak_extra_over_tables=32.00 GiB load_time=1.593 s weight_all_zero=False scale_bytes=[120]\n# this PR\npeak_extra_over_tables=0.00 GiB load_time=0.041 s weight_all_zero=True scale_bytes=[120]\n```\n\n`pre-commit` (ruff, mypy) passes on the changed files.\n\nNot tested: dummy loading of the full model.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
